# Five accessibility fixes fumadocs-ui 16.15.2 does not ship: a localized name
# for the legal pages' header navigation (#305), and the four roles and names
# axe reported on every docs page (#308), plus the copy buttons' own `lang`
# (#308 review).
#
# HISTORY
# -------
# Ported from `patches/fumadocs-ui@16.8.12.patch` (#314, #317) when
# `fumadocs-ui` moved to 16.15.2 in lockstep with `fumadocs-core` (dependabot
# #239). That patch had thirteen hunks. Eight of them backported upstream
# 16.9.0's own fix for nine icon-button names that 16.8.12 hard-coded in English
# outside its Translations API ("Open Search", "Toggle Theme", "Open Sidebar",
# "Collapse Sidebar", "Copy Anchor Link", "Copy Text", "Copied Text", "Toggle
# Menu"). They are DROPPED: 16.15.2 reads every one of those names through its
# Translations API, as `t("Open Search", { note: "aria-label" })` under a
# `useTranslations({ note: "search trigger" })` and so on (the keys are listed
# in its `dist/.translations/keys.js`), and `apps/docs/lib/ui-text.ts` supplies
# them under those keys. The five hunks below are the ones upstream still does
# not have; each anchor was re-checked against the 16.15.2 tarball.
#
# WHAT THIS CHANGES
# -----------------
# - layouts/home/slots/header.js (`navMain`, #305): Radix's NavigationMenu root
#   defaults `aria-label="Main"`, and the HomeLayout header (the privacy and
#   terms pages here) renders that root without a label of its own, so every
#   locale announced "Main". The root now reads its name through the same
#   Translations API as the rest of the header, as `t("Main", { note:
#   "aria-label" })` under `useTranslations({ note: "navigation menu" })`, so
#   its key is "Main(navigation menu)(aria-label)". The key also joins
#   `dist/.translations/keys.js` and the `Translations` type in
#   `dist/.translations/index.d.ts`, which is what makes a lost hunk loud (see
#   below). With no translation the name is still "Main".
# - layouts/shared/slots/language-select.js (#308, WCAG 2.5.3 label in name):
#   the trigger shows the current language ("English", "Deutsch") and was named
#   "Choose a language" only, so its name did not contain its text. It is now
#   named "<current language> — <Choose a language>": "English — Choose a
#   language", "Deutsch — Sprache wählen". The visible text comes first, and
#   both halves come from the i18n context, so every locale gets its own words
#   with no new key. With no current name in the locale list it keeps the old
#   label. A `slots.languageSelect.root` override per layout could do the same,
#   but a layout added later would quietly not; the patch reaches every trigger.
# - layouts/shared/index.js (#308, axe `svg-img-alt`): the GitHub icon
#   `githubUrl` adds was an `svg role="img"` with no name. Every link that
#   renders it carries `aria-label` "GitHub", so the picture is decorative:
#   `aria-hidden` replaces `role="img"`.
# - components/codeblock.js (#308, axe `landmark-unique`): every code block's
#   scroll viewport was `role="region"` with no name. The role goes and
#   `tabIndex: 0` stays, so the viewport still scrolls from the keyboard.
#   Naming each one was rejected: an untitled block has nothing to be named by,
#   titles repeat within a page, and ten code landmarks bury a page's real
#   landmarks. The role is set after `...viewportProps`, so no prop can remove
#   it; hence a hunk.
# - layouts/docs/page/slots/toc.js (#308, axe `landmark-unique` below 1280px):
#   the table-of-contents bar shown below 1280px (`xl:hidden`) was a `<header>`
#   outside every sectioning element, a second banner landmark beside the site
#   header. It is a disclosure for the page's headings, so it is a `<div>`. No
#   CSS selects `header` by element. The options reach only the bar's outer
#   wrapper, so this too is a hunk.
# - components/codeblock.js and components/heading.js (#308 review, WCAG
#   3.1.2): on a fallback page the heading-anchor and code-copy buttons sit in
#   a body `app/[lang]/docs/[[...slug]]/page.tsx` marks `lang="en"`, so their
#   localized names were read with English rules. Both buttons take `locale`
#   from `useI18n()` and render it as their own `lang`.
#   `check-locale-surface.mjs` (`localized-name-marked-english`) reads it off
#   the built pages.
#
# The #308 finding "no main landmark" needs neither a hunk nor app code any
# more: 16.15.2's DocsPage container renders `<main className="contents">`
# around its `<article>`, so the `role="main"` the docs page used to set on
# that article was removed with this port (two main landmarks otherwise).
#
# WHEN THIS FILE CAN BE DELETED
# -----------------------------
# When every hunk below is upstream. On a bump, re-check each anchor against
# the new tarball and drop the hunks whose fix upstream ships.
#
# What makes a silent loss loud: `fumadocsTranslations()` in
# `apps/docs/lib/ui-text.ts` returns an object literal typed as fumadocs'
# `Translations`, and it supplies "Main(navigation menu)(aria-label)"; on an
# install without this patch that key is an excess-property error and `tsc`
# fails `type-check` (measured while porting: with the 16.15.2 patch committed
# but not yet installed, `type-check` failed with TS2353 on exactly that key).
# The English-name half is read off the built pages by
# `check-locale-surface.mjs` (`english-chrome-name`). And as with the
# fumadocs-core pin beside this one, a bump of the package without regenerating
# this file fails `pnpm install` with ERR_PNPM_UNUSED_PATCH, which is what sends
# the person bumping it here.
#
